        "label": "Envelope and pores",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Envelope + pores",
        "lines": [
          "The nucleus was discovered by Robert Brown.",
          "It is bounded by a nuclear envelope of two",
          "membranes with a perinuclear space between",
          "them, and the outer membrane is continuous",
          "with the endoplasmic reticulum.",
          "Nuclear pores in the envelope let materials",
          "pass between the nucleus and the cytoplasm."
        ],
        "why": "Two membranes and the pores through them are what make the nucleus a separate compartment that can still exchange material with the cytoplasm.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that the nuclear envelope is a single membrane. It has two.",
          "Writing that the envelope is completely closed. It is porous."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Two membranes, one gap, many pores — and the outer one runs straight into the ER.",
        "margin_note": "Robert Brown and 'two membranes' open the answer."
