      {
        "id": "s3_nucleolus",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Nucleoplasm and nucleolus",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Nucleolus",
        "lines": [
          "The ground substance inside the envelope is",
          "the nucleoplasm.",
          "It contains one or more nucleoli.",
          "A nucleolus is not bound by a membrane. It is",
          "the site of active ribosomal RNA synthesis,",
          "and ribosomes are assembled there."
        ],
        "why": "The nucleolus is where ribosomal RNA is made, so a cell that makes a great deal of protein has a large nucleolus. That link is why the structure is marked.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that the nucleolus is membrane bound. It is not.",
          "Writing that the nucleolus makes DNA. It makes ribosomal RNA."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Nucleolus and ribosome start the same story: rRNA is made here.",
